Z||000000||Cyberkhat||11-25-2001||07:41 PM||||Howdy forum - I just joined this list and can see it is going to be VERY usefull.OK - I bought an 87 GT in July that I am ready to pull the 2.8 out of.Should I build this engine (53000 miles - good shape)or chuck it and go w/ the 3.4 block? I want to do a mild performance enhancement either way. I'll let this site make my choice..... You gotta love a site devoted to P car fans.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-25-2001||10:48 PM||||If you want a mild performance engine go with the 3.4.  It should be more reliable than the 2.8, if you want to push it.  Its hard to tell what condition the 2.8 with 53K miles is in.  I bought an 88 with 54000 on the odometer and the engine was trashed.<P>If the 2.8 engine has been maintained, I know people who have over 200K miles on them.<P>It all depends on the green stuff to get it done right or your skill to do it right.||||reg||1
